  The process:

  1. ONE loss measures total error: 0.8
  2. Calculus calculates gradients for EVERY weight:
    - All attention network weights (61,568 of them)
    - All classifier weights (however many there are)
    - Each gradient says: "change me by this amount to reduce loss"
  3. ALL weights update simultaneously:
  attention_weight_1 = attention_weight_1 - (learning_rate × gradient_1)
  attention_weight_2 = attention_weight_2 - (learning_rate × gradient_2)
  ...
  classifier_weight_1 = classifier_weight_1 - (learning_rate × gradient_1)
  classifier_weight_2 = classifier_weight_2 - (learning_rate × gradient_2)
  ...
  4. Next batch → new loss → new gradients → update again
  5. Repeat thousands of times → loss gets smaller → model gets better!

  ---
  Everyone works together to minimize the SAME loss!

  Attention learns: "Make better summary vectors to help reduce loss"
  Classifier learns: "Make better predictions to reduce loss"

